This licence covers what is actually ours in this repository: the pipeline
driver, the Win16 runtime and shims, the tools, the build files and the
documentation. It does NOT cover Bang! Bang! itself.

Bang! Bang! (1990) is a Windows 3.0 cannon-fire game and is not ours to
license. Its executable, help file, resources and art are not in this
repository and are excluded by .gitignore. Shareware is not public domain: a
1990 shareware release still carries its author's copyright.

Two consequences worth being explicit about:

  * You need your own copy of BANGBANG.EXE to use any of this. Drop it in
    original/ and the pipeline reads it from there.

  * Lifted code is a derivative work of the binary it came from. Anything this
    pipeline emits into src/recomp/ carries whatever licence the original
    carries, not this one. The MIT grant above stops at the tools.
